  "title": "Line-by-line redaction leaves multiline credentials in failure excerpts",
  "file": "src/gates/run.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "If a registered credential contains a line break, each half is checked for redaction on its own line, so neither half matches. The failure excerpt then joins the lines back together, and the full secret is stored and sent to models. Registered credentials are provider API keys read one line at a time from secrets.env, so a multiline value would be very unusual.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun $TMPDIR/c1.ts  (registers \"synthetic-key-line-one\\nsynthetic-key-line-two\", feeds `error: <secret>\\n(fail) assertion` line by line through redactGateOutput into FailureExcerpts)",
    "output": "combined redacted: true\nexcerpt leaks: true"
   },
   "evidence": "src/gates/run.ts:72-77 `const observe = (line: string) => { confinementError ||= launchFailure(line); line = redactGateOutput(line); coverage.observe(line); excerpts.observe(line); }`. Redaction runs on one line at a time. FailureExcerpts.finish then joins the lines with \"\\n\". redactCredentials (proc.ts:554) only matches whole literal values. The credentials come from config.ts:182, which reads the line-based parseEnvFile, so values with newlines can only come from the environment."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A failing check prints a registered credential spanning two lines. The failure excerpt reconstructs the complete credential and exposes it through saved results and model feedback.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/adjudicate-gate-output.ts\"",
    "output": "C1 {\"output\":\"error: credential [redacted]\\n(fail) assertion\",\"failures\":\"error: credential synthetic-private-key-line1\\nsynthetic-private-key-line2\\n(fail) assertion\",\"excerptLeaksCompleteCredential\":true,\"feedbackLeaksCompleteCredential\":true}"
   },
   "evidence": "The temporary probe exercised HEAD's actual runGates and real subprocess output, bypassing only confinement and scratch allocation. HEAD calls 'line = redactGateOutput(line)' before 'excerpts.observe(line)', so neither individual line contains the complete registered value. FailureExcerpts subsequently joins retained lines with '\\n'; runOne returns 'excerpts.result()' without another redaction pass. Base also leaked multiline credentials, but the request explicitly requires redaction before failure-excerpt extraction."
  }
