  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A check prints a credential followed by enough terminal formatting to cross the process runner's output limit. The runner drops the credential's prefix, and formatting removal exposes its unredacted suffix in the saved gate output.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/adjudicate-gate-output.ts\"",
    "output": "C2 {\"ok\":true,\"output\":\"y-credential-409\",\"leakedSuffix\":\"y-credential-409\",\"suffixLeaked\":true}"
   },
   "evidence": "The temporary probe exercised HEAD's actual runGates with real subprocess output and confinement/scratch bypassed. It printed a registered credential followed by 15,996 copies of ESC[0m. src/util/proc.ts sets DEFAULT_TAIL = 64_000 and truncates with 'next.slice(next.length - limit)' before runOne receives the result. HEAD then calls 'redactGateOutput(`${res.stdout}\\n${res.stderr}`)', which cannot match the remaining suffix. The deploy gate likewise redacts already-bounded process results at service.ts:450-451. Base had the same upstream truncation, but the requested fix explicitly requires redaction before truncation."
  }
 },
